From b6dfe8b318b041b355f25220d0d11af632d5c9b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gyp: build node as gnu++20, like the V8 archives

G5 nodejs22 build 2026-09-02, item #2 (right after the abseil target
was dropped): every TU that includes deps/ncrypto/ncrypto.h fails at

  ncrypto.h:367:7: error: declaration of 'operator<=' as non-function
    367 |   int operator<=>(const BignumPointer& other) const noexcept;

ncrypto.h declares operator<=> unguarded.  gcc only lexes <=> as one
token from C++20 on; under the port's gnu++17 pin (patch 0001) it reads
`operator<=` followed by `>`.  Reproduced with gcc 13 -std=gnu++17
(same text) and accepted with -std=gnu++20.  Upstream 22.23.2 pins
gnu++17 on posix and mac (common.gypi:514, :694) and C++20 only on
Windows ("needed for V8 v12.4+"); clang takes the spaceship token as an
extension in C++17 mode, which is how the upstream clang builds get
past this header.

Switch the gcc pin to gnu++20: the standard the v8-12.4 port built the
archives with (compiler.cxx_standard 2020), so the headers node shares
with V8 - v8.h, cppgc, absl - are compiled under the same language
mode.  Node itself is C++20-clean (the Windows build).  -fpermissive
stays.  No change to the gyp graph: this is the same xcode_settings
entry the 09-01 rig showed flowing into every C++ compile line, only
the value changes.

On the G5: gyp's generated make rules re-run any command whose text
changed, so the C++ objects compiled so far under gnu++17 are rebuilt
with gnu++20 automatically; C objects are untouched.
---
 common.gypi | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common.gypi b/common.gypi
index b56afd6..a3da08c 100644
--- a/common.gypi
+++ b/common.gypi
@@ -712,20 +712,22 @@
           }],
           # Pin the C++ standard: the CLANG_CXX_LANGUAGE_STANDARD below is
           # clang-only, and without an explicit -std modern gcc defaults to
-          # gnu++17 (gcc 11-15) or gnu++23 (gcc 16+).  gnu++17 is what
-          # upstream builds node with on every posix platform; the external
-          # V8 archives are gnu++20, which is link-compatible, and the V8
-          # public headers compile as C++17.
+          # gnu++17 (gcc 11-15) or gnu++23 (gcc 16+).  gnu++20 is the
+          # standard the external V8 archives were built with.  Upstream
+          # pins gnu++17 here, but deps/ncrypto/ncrypto.h declares
+          # operator<=>, which gcc only lexes as one token from C++20 on
+          # (clang accepts it as an extension in C++17 mode), and node is
+          # already built as C++20 on Windows for V8 12.4.
           ['target_arch=="ppc"', {
             'xcode_settings': {
               'ARCHS': ['ppc'],
-              'OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS': ['-std=gnu++17', '-fpermissive'],
+              'OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS': ['-std=gnu++20', '-fpermissive'],
             },
           }],
           ['target_arch=="ppc64"', {
             'xcode_settings': {
               'ARCHS': ['ppc64'],
-              'OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS': ['-std=gnu++17', '-fpermissive'],
+              'OTHER_CPLUSPLUSFLAGS': ['-std=gnu++20', '-fpermissive'],
             },
           }],
           ['clang==1', {
